{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k smallest eigenvalues of the Laplacian L ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"laplacianMatrix()"},{"type":"text","text":"), k = "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ascending, each with a unit eigenvector (see ","type":"text"},{"code":"Eigenpairs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"laplacianEigenpairs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"smallest","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-8, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Eigenpairs","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory10EigenpairsV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of eigenpairs, in "},{"code":"0...vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"name":"smallest"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The residual a Ritz pair must reach, relative as described above.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"tolerance"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for the limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under Throws.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"maxIterations"}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Component by component: each component’s null vector first (eigenvalue 0, components in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order of their least vertex), then the smallest positive eigenvalues of the components","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"merged. On a component of at least 64 vertices, thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reorthogonalization and locking, the null vector projected out, from a fixed start vector:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on σI − M (σ Gershgorin’s bound) while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on M⁺ by shift-invert, each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"product a conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pair is accepted when its residual is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" · λ, relative to itself as for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"algebraicConnectivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the vectors found are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value is its vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The dense solver on a smaller","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component, or when k is a third of it or more.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10) for the basis.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"smallest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0...vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when given, is at least 1.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note"},{"name":"Throws","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" when a Lanczos run by shift-invert spends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" products"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1,000 when nil), or a conjugate-gradient solve inside it 20,000 + 2n iterations, without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converging. A run on σI − M hands over to shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"20√n products or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", whichever is smaller. The dense solver throws as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"laplacianSpectrum"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Gr